From: ONIE maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] loader/bsd: return an explicit error when metadata allocation fails

On failure the output pointer is not assigned. Return a guaranteed nonzero
error instead of relying on global grub_errno, so GCC 14 can prove that
successful callers always receive an initialized metadata pointer.

--- a/grub-core/loader/i386/bsd.c
+++ b/grub-core/loader/i386/bsd.c
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@
 
   newtag = grub_malloc (len + sizeof (struct bsd_tag));
   if (!newtag)
-    return grub_errno;
+    return grub_error (GRUB_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY, "cannot allocate BSD metadata");
   newtag->len = len;
   newtag->type = type;
   newtag->next = NULL;
